//// `String.fromCodepoint` of a value that is no Unicode scalar value aborts
//// the program on every target (decision 262): erlang's `<<Cp/utf8>>` raises
//// `badarg`, the Node cell throws a `RangeError` (native
//// `String.fromCodePoint` would answer a lone surrogate) and wasm's
//// `$__str_from_cp` traps. What was printed before stays printed.

pub fn main() {
    @print("before");
    @print(String.fromCodepoint(55296));
    @print("after");
}
